[0] force FAIL by default to avoid IMPORTANT message below.
#1: Enter operator initials and PCB serial number:
a. Enter operator intials.
b. Enter serial number into the box below.
IMPORTANT: Observe ESD precautions for handling ESD sensitive devices.  
DISPLAY: PCB 287-027.png



#2: Setup equipment 1
a. Set adjustable PSU output 1 to 12V ±0.1V, 0.5A ±0.1A. Switch the output off.
b. Using TE159, connect the PSU to the Peripheral lighting PCB Test Jig (TE132).
c. Connect the PC (via USB) to the Peripheral lighting PCB Test Jig(TE132).
d. Connect the USB cable to the K5 on the Peripheral lighting PCB Test Jig(TE132).

DISPLAY: TE132.jpg
CLICK_OK:


#3: Setup equipment:
a. Connect the TE192 Test box to the TE132 Peripheral lighting PCB Test Jig.   
b. Connect the PCB to the TE192 Test box.
c. Connect the TE086 (LED Test Box with Web Camera) to the PC and place the PCB inside.
d. Switch the output of the adjustable PSU on and power on the TE132 Peripheral lighting PCB Test Jig. 
//DISPLAY: Setup.jpg
COMMENT: *Example image below*
CLICK_OK:
CONNECT: MLPRO2 
COMMAND: MLPRO2 If#	// turn off any LEDs still on: 
IF_NOT:
GOTO: #2


#4: PCB communication check
COMMAND: MLPRO2  BENUM
READLINE: MLPRO2  BENUM
IF:
Check the expected result is a match.
Expected result is = RS,RS1,RS2
.
..
...

Returned result is = %BENUM%
ELSE:
Bad result . . . sorry
PASS_FAIL: #4
EXE: OpenWinCam.bat


#5: RING LIGHT LED  = RED
a. Check for 4 LED hot spots
COMMAND: MLPRO2 RING 100000 650
DELAY: 750
PASS_FAIL: #5

#6: RING LIGHT LED = BLUEGREEN
a. Check for 4 LED hot spots
COMMAND: MLPRO2 RING 001000 650
DELAY: 700
PASS_FAIL: #6

#7: RING LIGHT LED = VIOLET
a. Check for 4 LED hot spots
COMMAND: MLPRO2 RING 000010 650
DELAY: 700
PASS_FAIL: #7

#8: RING LIGHT LED = UV
a. Check for 4 LED hot spots
COMMAND: MLPRO2 RING 000001 650
DELAY: 700
PASS_FAIL: #8

#9: RING LIGHT LED = GREEN
a. Check for 4 LED hot spots
COMMAND: MLPRO2 RING 07000 650
DELAY: 700
PASS_FAIL: #9

#10: RING LIGHT LED = BLUE
a. Check for 4 LED hot spots
COMMAND: MLPRO2 RING 000100 650
DELAY: 700
PASS_FAIL: #10

#12: Test complete:
EXE: CloseWinCam.bat
COMMAND: MLPRO2 If#	// turn off any LEDs still on: 
a. All tests instructions have been completed and a log file created.
b. Click OK to finish and then power off the PSU and disconnect the PCB.
